changeSet.sql:
COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.frecency.chunk_id IS
  'No FK, by GRAIN, not by deferral (RDR-194 D7). nexus.chunks is keyed (tenant_id, collection, chash); frecency has no collection column -- its PK is (tenant_id, chunk_id), one row per chash per tenant ACROSS collections by design. Adding a collection column to make an FK expressible would change the table''s identity grain, a behaviour change, not hygiene. The standing detection for this edge is the nexus_diag debt view nexus.diag_chash_conformance (observe-only for this table; src/nexus/db/chash_tables.py). The engine-side ChashCensus leg this comment used to name was deleted at nexus-z0o2p.27 together with its only caller; D0.10''s one-for-one FK retirement does not fire here.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN nexus.relevance_log.chunk_id IS
  'No FK, by GRAIN, not by deferral (RDR-194 D7) -- the same reasoning as nexus.frecency.chunk_id: nexus.chunks is keyed (tenant_id, collection, chash) and relevance_log has no collection column, so an FK is not expressible without changing the table''s identity grain. The standing detection for this edge is the nexus_diag debt view nexus.diag_chash_conformance (observe-only for this table; src/nexus/db/chash_tables.py). The engine-side ChashCensus leg this comment used to name was deleted at nexus-z0o2p.27 together with its only caller; D0.10''s one-for-one FK retirement does not fire here.';

